module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Pullbacks
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.QuasiRegular
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheafAffine.Regular
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularImmersion.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeQuasiRegularFibre.Stalk

/-!
# A quasi-regular ideal sheaf is regular, reduced to two residues

Stacks tag 063U says that an immersion `i : Z ⟶ X` which is relatively quasi-regular over a base
`f : X ⟶ S` that is flat and locally of finite presentation is a regular immersion, and stays
one after an arbitrary base change. **Both assertions of the tag are proved unconditionally
elsewhere** — the first is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isRegularImmersion_of_isRelativeQuasiRegular`
`Immersion` in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RegularImmersion/Relative.lean` and the second is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isRegularImmersion_baseChange_of_isRelativeQuasiRegularImmersion` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RegularImmersion/BaseChange.lean`, both carrying the `063U`
attribute — by spreading out over an affine open rather than point by point.

What this file keeps is the *pointwise* route to the same conclusion at the level of ideal
sheaves, which is a different decomposition of the argument: it reduces regularity of a
quasi-regular ideal sheaf to two named residues, and proves everything on either side of them.
The residues themselves are the interface that
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/QuotientStalk/Basic.lean` discharges the first half of.

Both sides of the implication are already reduced to the same shape. Tag 063G produces, near each
point of the support of the quotient, an affine open and generators of the defining ideal which
are quasi-regular in the ring of sections, and whose germs therefore satisfy the elementary
relation condition at every point of that open; and tag 063D part (1) asks of the regular side
exactly that the germ of each generator carry nothing into the ideal of the germs of its
predecessors, at **every** point of a witness open. So the whole content is the passage from
quasi-regular to regular, index by index and point by point. Splitting on the position of the
first unit of the sequence in the stalk at the point leaves exactly three cases:

* some germ of `g j` with `j ≤ i` is a unit. Then the condition at `i` is free —
  `isRegularRel_of_isUnit_le`. Below the unit the ideal of the predecessors is everything, and at
  it the member is itself a unit.
* every germ of `g` lies in the maximal ideal, that is, the point lies on the immersed subscheme.
  Then the whole sequence of germs is regular, by the local step of tag 0470 proved in
  `RelativeQuasiRegularFibre/Stalk.lean`, whose four instance hypotheses are discharged from the
  structural morphism alone — provided the quotient of the stalk by the germs is flat over the
  stalk of the base. That hypothesis is the **first residue**, `QuotientStalkFlat`.
* every germ of `g j` with `j ≤ i` lies in the maximal ideal, and some later germ is a unit. This
  is a point off the immersed subscheme at which an initial segment of the generators still
  vanishes, and there quasi-regularity asserts nothing whatever: the generators span the unit
  ideal in the stalk, and `QuasiRegularUnitIdeal.isQuasiRegular_cons_one` exhibits a quasi-regular
  sequence spanning the unit ideal whose first member is a zero divisor. The source shrinks the
  open set here, and that is the **second residue**, `RegularityShrinksOffSubscheme`.

Everything else is proved. `isRegularIdealSheaf_of_isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf` is the complete
argument given the two residues.

## Main results

* `isRegularRel_of_isUnit_le`: at and above the first unit of a sequence the regularity condition
  of tag 063D holds for free.
* `isRegularRel_germFamily_of_isQuasiRegular`: the local step of tag 063U at a point of the
  immersed subscheme, taking as input exactly the affine data that tag 063G produces.
* `QuotientStalkFlat`, `RegularityShrinksOffSubscheme`: the two residues, each with a docstring
  saying what would discharge it.
* `isRegularIdealSheaf_of_isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf`: tag 063U for ideal sheaves, given the two
  residues.

## Implementation notes

The vocabulary throughout is the relation form `Stacks.RingTheory.RegularIdealSheafAffine`
supplies: `IsRegularRel x I` says that `x` carries nothing into `I` from outside `I`, and
`precedingIdeal` and `precedingFamilyIdeal` are the ideals generated by the members, respectively
the germs, strictly preceding a given index. `isRegularSequenceOn_iff_isRegularRel` is the
germwise reading of the sheaf condition in that vocabulary and `isWeaklyRegular_ofFn_iff` the
translation to Mathlib's `RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular`, which is what the local
step of tag 0470 concludes. `precedingIdeal (germFamily X U g y hy) i` and
`precedingFamilyIdeal X U g i y hy` have the same body, so no transport is needed between them.

The ambient scheme of an immersion is `i.coborderRange.toScheme`, the canonical open on which `i`
becomes the closed immersion `i.liftCoborder`; its structural morphism is `i.coborderRange.ι ≫ f`,
flat and locally of finite presentation by composition because `i.coborderRange.ι` is an open
immersion.

Tag 063G returns an *affine* open, and the local step needs that affineness, so the affine open
`U` is kept throughout and only the open on which generation is asserted is shrunk;
`germFamily_res` and `precedingFamilyIdeal_res` carry the germwise data across the restriction.

The hypothesis `Flat (i ≫ f)` of tag 063S — the half of relative quasi-regularity that is about
the base — is **not** used below. It is precisely what would discharge the first residue, through
the identification of the quotient of `𝒪_{X, y}` by the germs of the generators with the stalk
`𝒪_{Z, y}`; that identification is not available here and is the reason the residue is stated
rather than proved.

## What is not done

No `stacks` attribute is attached: along this route both residues are still hypotheses rather
than theorems, so nothing here proves tag 063U. The tag itself is proved, by the other route, in
`RegularImmersion/Relative.lean` and `RegularImmersion/BaseChange.lean`, and those are where its
attribute sits.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 10.99.3 (Tag 0470)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0470)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 15.47.5 (Tag 0CEP)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CEP)
* [Stacks Project, Definition 31.20.1 (Tag 063D)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063D)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.20.2 (Tag 063G)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063G)
* [Stacks Project, Definition 31.21.1 (Tag 063J)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063J)
* [Stacks Project, Definition 31.22.1 (Tag 063S)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063S)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.18.9 (Tag 062Y)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/062Y)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.23.4 (Tag 063U)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063U)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction
open Stacks.RingTheory.RegularIdealSheaf
open Stacks.RingTheory.RegularIdealSheafAffine
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular hiding germSequence
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheafAffine
open Stacks.RingedSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag063URegularImmersion

section Ring

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- The elementary relation form of quasi-regularity is quasi-regularity of the sequence. -/
theorem isQuasiRegular_of_isQuasiRegularRel {r : ℕ} (g : Fin r → A) (h : IsQuasiRegularRel g) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsQuasiRegular A (List.ofFn g) :=
  (isQuasiRegular_ofFn_iff g).2 ((isQuasiRegularRel_iff_bijective g).1 h)

/-- **At and above the first unit of a sequence the regularity condition of Stacks tag 063D is
automatic.** If some member `g j` with `j ≤ i` is a unit then `g i` carries nothing into the
ideal of the predecessors of `g i` from outside it: for `j < i` that ideal contains a unit and is
therefore everything, and for `j = i` the member itself is a unit. -/
theorem isRegularRel_of_isUnit_le {r : ℕ} (g : Fin r → A) (i j : Fin r) (hji : j ≤ i)
    (hu : IsUnit (g j)) : IsRegularRel (g i) (precedingIdeal g i) := by
  rcases eq_or_lt_of_le hji with rfl | hlt
  · exact fun a ha => ((precedingIdeal g j).unit_mul_mem_iff_mem hu).mp ha
  · have hmem : g j ∈ precedingIdeal g i := Ideal.subset_span ⟨⟨j.val, hlt⟩, rfl⟩
    intro a _
    rw [Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _ hmem hu]
    exact Submodule.mem_top

end Ring

section Pointwise

/-- **The local step of Stacks tag 063U at a point of the immersed subscheme, from the affine
data that Stacks tag 063G produces.** Let `p : X ⟶ S` be flat and locally of finite presentation,
let `U` be an affine open of `X` and let `g` be a sequence of sections over `U` which is
quasi-regular in `Γ(X, U)`. At a point `y` of `U` at which every germ of `g` lies in the maximal
ideal, and at which the quotient of the stalk by the germs of `g` is flat over the stalk of `S`,
the germ of each `g i` carries nothing into the ideal of the germs of its predecessors from
outside it. -/
theorem isRegularRel_germFamily_of_isQuasiRegular {S X : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ S) [Flat p]
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation p] (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {r : ℕ}
    (g : Fin r → Γ(X, U))
    (hqr : RingTheory.Sequence.IsQuasiRegular Γ(X, U) (List.ofFn g)) (y : X) (hy : y ∈ U)
    (hmem : ∀ j, germFamily X.toRingedSpace U g y hy j ∈
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk y))
    (hflat : ((Ideal.Quotient.mk
        (Ideal.span (Set.range (germFamily X.toRingedSpace U g y hy)))).comp
          (p.stalkMap y).hom).Flat) (i : Fin r) :
    IsRegularRel (germFamily X.toRingedSpace U g y hy i)
      (precedingFamilyIdeal X.toRingedSpace U g i y hy) :=
  (isWeaklyRegular_ofFn_iff _).1
    (RelativeQuasiRegularFibre.isRegular_germ_of_isQuasiRegular p y
      (germFamily X.toRingedSpace U g y hy) hmem
      (isQuasiRegular_of_isQuasiRegularRel _
        ((forall_isQuasiRegularRel_germ_iff X U hU g).2 hqr y hy)) hflat).toIsWeaklyRegular i

end Pointwise

section Residues

/-- **The first residue of Stacks tag 063U: flatness of the quotients of the stalks.** At a point
of the immersed subscheme — a point at which every germ of the generators lies in the maximal
ideal — the quotient of the stalk by those germs is flat over the stalk of the base.

For the defining ideal of an immersion `i : Z ⟶ X` with `Z ⟶ S` flat this is what flatness of
`i ≫ f` supplies, once the quotient of `𝒪_{X, y}` by the germs of the generators is identified
with the stalk `𝒪_{Z, y}`; the identification itself is not available here. -/
def QuotientStalkFlat {S X : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ S)
    (J : (structureSheafModule X.toRingedSpace).Submodule) : Prop :=
  ∀ (U : X.Opens) (r : ℕ) (g : Fin r → Γ(X, U)), IsGeneratedByOn X.toRingedSpace J U g →
    ∀ (y : X) (hy : y ∈ U),
      (∀ j, germFamily X.toRingedSpace U g y hy j ∈
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk y)) →
      ((Ideal.Quotient.mk
        (Ideal.span (Set.range (germFamily X.toRingedSpace U g y hy)))).comp
          (p.stalkMap y).hom).Flat

/-- **The second residue of Stacks tag 063U: the shrinking, at exactly the configuration that is
still owed.** Whenever the ideal sheaf `J` is generated near a point `x` of the support of
`𝒪_X / J` by a quasi-regular sequence of sections over an open `U`, there is a smaller
neighbourhood `V` of `x` on which the germ of `g i` carries nothing into the ideal of the germs of
its predecessors, at every point `y` where

* every germ of `g j` with `j ≤ i` lies in the maximal ideal of `𝒪_{X, y}`, and
* some germ of `g` is a unit in `𝒪_{X, y}`, that is, `y` lies off the immersed subscheme.

Nothing outside that configuration is asked for, and nothing inside it is reachable from the
hypotheses as they stand. The points at which *every* germ lies in the maximal ideal are settled
without any shrinking by `isRegularRel_germFamily_of_isQuasiRegular`, and the indices `i` for
which some earlier or equal `g j` is a unit are free by `isRegularRel_of_isUnit_le`. What is left
is a point off the subscheme at which an initial segment of the generators still vanishes, and
there quasi-regularity is literally vacuous — the generators span the whole stalk, and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegularUnitIdeal.isQuasiRegular_cons_one` exhibits a quasi-regular
sequence spanning the unit ideal whose first member is a zero divisor. The source closes that gap
by shrinking: a regular sequence on the closed fibre `X_s` (Stacks tags 0CEP and 061S), spread
out inside the Noetherian fibre (tag 061L) and transported to a neighbourhood in `X` through the
relative effective Cartier divisor chain of tag 062Y. -/
def RegularityShrinksOffSubscheme (X : Scheme.{u})
    (J : (structureSheafModule X.toRingedSpace).Submodule) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : X, x ∈ idealQuotientSupport X.toRingedSpace J →
    ∀ (U : X.Opens) (_hxU : x ∈ U) (r : ℕ) (g : Fin r → Γ(X, U)),
      IsGeneratedByOn X.toRingedSpace J U g →
      RingTheory.Sequence.IsQuasiRegular Γ(X, U) (List.ofFn g) →
      ∃ (V : X.Opens) (_hxV : x ∈ V) (hVU : V ≤ U),
        ∀ (y : X) (hy : y ∈ V) (i : Fin r),
          (∀ j : Fin r, j ≤ i → germFamily X.toRingedSpace U g y (hVU hy) j ∈
            IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk y)) →
          (∃ j : Fin r, germFamily X.toRingedSpace U g y (hVU hy) j ∉
            IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk y)) →
          IsRegularRel (germFamily X.toRingedSpace U g y (hVU hy) i)
            (precedingFamilyIdeal X.toRingedSpace U g i y (hVU hy))

/-- **Stacks tag 063U at the level of ideal sheaves, reduced to its two residues.** A
quasi-regular ideal sheaf on a scheme flat and locally of finite presentation over the base is
regular, given flatness of the quotients of the stalks at the points of the subscheme and the
shrinking at the points off it. -/
theorem isRegularIdealSheaf_of_isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf {S X : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ S) [Flat p]
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation p] (J : (structureSheafModule X.toRingedSpace).Submodule)
    (hJ : IsQuasiRegularIdealSheaf X.toRingedSpace J) (hflat : QuotientStalkFlat p J)
    (hshrink : RegularityShrinksOffSubscheme X J) :
    IsRegularIdealSheaf X.toRingedSpace J := by
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, r, g, hgen, hqr⟩ :=
    (isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf_iff_exists_affine_generators X J).1 hJ x hx
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, hVU, hoff⟩ := hshrink x hx U.1 hxU r g hgen hqr
  refine ⟨V, hxV, r, fun j => X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op (g j), ?_,
    isGeneratedByOn_of_le U.1 g hgen V hVU⟩
  rw [isRegularSequenceOn_iff_isRegularRel]
  intro i y hy
  rw [precedingFamilyIdeal_res X.toRingedSpace U.1 g V hVU i y hy,
    germFamily_res U.1 V hVU g y hy]
  by_cases hle : ∀ j : Fin r, j ≤ i → germFamily X.toRingedSpace U.1 g y (hVU hy) j ∈
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk y)
  · by_cases hall : ∀ j : Fin r, germFamily X.toRingedSpace U.1 g y (hVU hy) j ∈
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk y)
    · exact isRegularRel_germFamily_of_isQuasiRegular p U.1 U.2 g hqr y (hVU hy) hall
        (hflat U.1 r g hgen y (hVU hy) hall) i
    · exact hoff y hy i hle (not_forall.1 hall)
  · obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := not_forall.1 hle
    exact isRegularRel_of_isUnit_le _ i j (not_imp.1 hj).1
      (IsLocalRing.notMem_maximalIdeal.1 (not_imp.1 hj).2)

end Residues

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag063URegularImmersion

end
